            Every clear sealer in our test began showing gray within seven to eleven months. Every semi-transparent product with pigment lasted two to three times longer before needing attention. The mechanism is simple: pigment particles absorb and scatter UV before it reaches the lignin, and no amount of resin quality substitutes for that.
          </p>

