            The <strong class="text-white">best exterior wood sealer</strong> in two years of testing was <strong class="text-white">TWP 1500</strong>, still beading water at 22 months with no graying and a clean, strip-free recoat. If you have never sealed a deck before, <strong class="text-white">Ready Seal</strong> is nearly as durable and far harder to apply badly. For water-based, <strong class="text-white">DEFY Extreme</strong> holds color better than anything else in that category.
